{"kind":"artifact","text":"internal/app at exact clean pushed head 2df37050b990d59013ba9d119d3faae0c966148e on request/config-cross-process-cas, answering 9da2d677 under my promise 91c51d48.\n\nsave() is deleted. Every configuration mutation in this package now goes through Workspace.mutateConfig, which calls the apphost transaction and adopts only the two mutable fields under configMu. AddActor re-checks its duplicate-name condition against the freshly read state rather than against memory; RetireActor treats an absent-on-disk actor as unchanged; rememberVerifiedFrontier judges rollback, descent and depth against the stored frontier, with the same-head case reporting unchanged and storing nothing. The rollback guarantees on AddActor and RetireActor are unchanged, no keys are regenerated, and the failure modes they already had are preserved rather than quietly improved.\n\nOne consequence is embraced rather than hidden. Deleting the memory-first fast path means a workspace whose stored witness is unreachable now fails closed even when nothing changed. The existing test asserting the opposite embodied the contract codex rejected, so it is rewritten to assert the new one rather than kept green.\n\nThe cross-process fact at this layer is proven by a real second process: a child re-executes, opens the workspace and adds an actor, then the stale parent advances its frontier, and both the custody row and the key file must survive. That test is sequential rather than overlapped, which is the observed defects actual shape, and its comment says so rather than claiming an overlap it does not have.","body":{"commit":"2df37050b990d59013ba9d119d3faae0c966148e","path":"internal/app"}}